$C1C4 Level4Map8 ; level 4 zone 8: 28 rows
$C2A4 Level4Map9 ; level 4 zone 9: 15 rows
$C31C b Tiles 16 ; 256 tiles of 4 x 4 char codes (16 bytes: 4 rows of 4), read by $AD76
> Tile T is at $C31C + 16T: rows top to bottom, 4 char codes a row. The char codes index the zone's char set (zone +0: set 0 bitmaps $7100 attributes $7900, set 1 bitmaps $7A00 attributes $8200).
@res levels/tiles.bin
$D31C b ObjectKinds 8 ; 72 object kinds, 8 bytes each, indexed by an object record's kind (+1)
> SpawnObjects $FD7D copies, for kind K at $D31C + 8K: +0 to slot +7, +1 to slot +8, +2-3 (the animation list, AnimLists, or a graphic address $6A80-$914B for kinds 4-21) to slot +4/+5 and +$12/+$13, +4-5 (the movement script, ObjectScripts; 0 for kinds 0-23) to slot +$14/+$15. $F7C3 reads +6 and +7 ($D322 + 8K). Kinds 0, 2, 3 and 71 are all zero. The meaning of +0, +1, +6 and +7 (sizes and hit boxes, it seems) is known only from the code.
@res levels/kinds.bin
$D55C b Zones 7 ; The 34 zones, 7 bytes: +0 char set, +1-2 map, +3-4 exits, +5-6 object list
> EnterZone $AC83 (IX = the record, C = the map row): +0 = 0 char set 0, else set 1 (attributes $79 or $82 patched into $A853 and $AA80); +1-2 the map ($ADB5); +3-4 the exit list (the operand of $AB93); +5-6 the object list (the operand of $FD7D). Levels 1-2 use set 0, levels 3-4 set 1.
