> SpawnObjects $FD7D (D = the first map row, E = the rows) starts at the first record whose +0 is D or more and spawns while +0 < D + E. +0 the map char row (bits 3-7) ; +1 the kind (ObjectKinds; bit 7 set: taken, never spawned again; NewGame $E2DC clears bit 7 in 365 five-byte groups from $D7FD: the 331 records and the 34 zone terminators); +2 flags (bit 1: the one special slot $EA8E, bit 2: slot +0 bit 7, the whole byte to slot +$0B); +3 the x (bits 3-7) and a row offset (bits 0-2); +4 a second x (bits 3-7) and row offset (bits 0-2), slot +$0C/+$1D.
> Each list ends with $FF and the 4 bytes "term", a 5-byte record of its own: the RES 7 loop steps over it.
