# ---- 40-b.ann
# fragment B: $E219-$F3FF

@module menu ; The menu, the control choice, the new game, quit and GAME OVER
@about The menu Menu $E219 prints the title, the four control methods and the credits, plays tune 5 and lights the chosen method's row until fire. Keys 1-4 (`$A103`, `$A10B`, `$A113`, `$A11B`) store the method in `$A14C` (0 keyboard, 1 Kempston, 2 cursor, 3 Sinclair) and click (`$AB18` with `$AB45`).
@about NewGame $E2DC clears the done flags of the level object lists, the level, the game-complete flag and the score, gives 6 lives, 6 bullets and 6 dynamite, prints the first level's intro text, plays tune 0 and waits for the fire key to be let go; StartLevel $E32C (module levels) then waits for fire.
@about Quit $E35A (Q in the main loop, or the last life lost) and GameOver $E35D (also the way out after the ending) print GAME OVER, play tune 6, wait for a press and go back to the menu.

$E219 c Menu ; The menu: title, control methods, credits; choose a method and start
> Waits until no key is pressed (`$A123` gives Z while fire or a key is down), plays tune 5 (`$A016`), clears the screen (`$AB03`) and prints three texts with `$AAE9`: ControlsText $EA1B at `$40EA`, TitleText $E9FB at `$4041`, CreditsText $EA51 at `$5047`.
> Then, every two frames, it lights the attribute row of the chosen method (DE the attribute address, C its width: `$58EE`/8, `$592E`/8, `$596E`/6, `$59AE`/8 for methods 0-3) by `$AB18` with the colour table `$AB3D`, and reads keys 1-4. A new method is stored in `$A14C` and its old row is put back with `$AB45`. Fire (`$A123` Z) leaves through MenuWaitRelease into NewGame $E2DC.
> Seen in c1, controls (all four methods), gameover, level1 and ending; the menu screen is work/images/menu.*.bin. The `LD DE,$780A` at `$E229` is dead: the next instruction loads DE again.
> Witness: L1 26072 (c1, controls, ending2, gameover, level1).
$E229 ; dead load: DE is set again at once
@isub $E229 LD DE,$780A
$E244 MenuLoop ; DE, C = the attribute row and width of the chosen method
$E266 MenuShowRow
$E267 MenuFrame ; two frames a pass
$E289 MenuTryKey2 ; 2: Kempston
$E2A1 MenuTryKey3 ; 3: cursor keys
$E2B9 MenuTryKey4 ; 4: Sinclair
$E2D1 MenuTestFire
$E2D7 MenuWaitRelease

$E2DC c NewGame ; New game: reset the game state, print the first level's intro
> Clears the screen, then bit 7 (done) of `$016D` records of 5 bytes from `$D7FD` (the level object lists: a taken or killed one-shot object stays gone), Level $E4AD, GameComplete $E440 and the score `$A9BE-$A9C3`. Lives `$A958`, bullets `$A976` and dynamite `$A967` = 6. `$A93D` draws the HUD.
> LevelIntro prints LevelTable's first text (SouthAmericaText $E4E5) at its screen address with `$AAE9`, C = `$47`, sets `$7900` to the record's attribute, plays tune 0 and waits until fire is let go; StartLevel $E32C follows.
> Run once per new game: c1 1, controls 4, gameover 1, level1 2 (the natural GAME OVER starts a new game).
> Witness: L1 9 (beeper48, c1, controls, gameover, level1).
$E2E8 ClearDoneLoop
$E311 LevelIntro ; LevelTable record 0: text, place, attribute
$E327 IntroWaitRelease

@module levels ; The level table and the first level's start
@about The level table LevelTable $E4AE holds 11 bytes a level: the intro text and where it goes, the attribute byte stored in `$7900`, Rick's x and y and the first zone record with its count for `$AC83`. Record 0 is the level being played: NewGame $E2DC and StartLevel $E32C read it; the level change `$ABF6` / `$AC07` reads record Level $E4AD, and record 4 is the closing text of the ending.
@about The level and zone change itself (`$AB93`, `$ABF6`, `$AC83`) lies outside this fragment.

$E32C c StartLevel ; Start the first level: wait for fire, place Rick, set up the first zone
> Waits for fire (`$A123` Z), then puts Rick at LevelTable's x and y (RickX $EAAD, RickY $EAAE), his size `$18` x `$15` (RickWidth $EAB3, RickHeight $EAB4), and sets up the zone with IX = the zone record and C = its count (`$AC83`).
> With lives left (always, at a new game) it goes on to NewLife $E3AF; with none it falls into Quit $E35A.
> Witness: L1 134127 (beeper48, c1, controls, gameover, level1-level4).

@module menu
$E35A c Quit ; Quit: Q in the main loop, or the last life lost
> Reached from MainLoop $E3C9 when `$A13C` gives Z (the Q key), from CheckDeath when the lives reach 0, and from StartLevel with no lives. Calls `$A73F`, then GAME OVER.
> Seen in c1 (Q), controls (Q after each method), gameover and level1 (six deaths).
> Witness: L1 8 (beeper48, c1, controls, gameover, level1).

$E35D c GameOver ; GAME OVER: print it, tune 6, wait for a key, back to the menu
> Calls `$A90F` and `$A25D`, prints GameOverBlankText $E397, GameOverText $E3A3 and GameOverBlankText again with `$AA8D` at `$484B`, `$486B`, `$488B` (attributes `$49`, `$4F`, `$49`), plays tune 6, waits until no key is down and then for a press, and jumps to Menu $E219.
> Also the end of the game: CheckGameComplete $E406 jumps here after the ending (the ending recording shows GAME OVER after the closing text).
> Witness: L1 9 (beeper48, c1, controls, ending2, gameover, level1).
$E389 GameOverWaitRelease
$E38E GameOverWaitPress

$E397 t GameOverBlankText ; 11 spaces, ended by $FF: the band above and below GAME OVER
@res texts/GameOverBlankText.bin
$E3A3 t GameOverText ; " GAME OVER ", ended by $FF
@res texts/GameOverText.bin

@module mainloop ; The main loop: one pass every 2 frames
@about MainLoop $E3C9 runs once a pass: the quit test (`$A13C`), UpdateObjects $EC11 (every object, Rick included), BonusCountdown $E466, the pause test (`$A144`), the death and zone-change tests, then HALT at MainLoopHalt $E40F and the drawing: `$A73F`, `$A144`, `$A22A` with C = 1, `$A25D`, `$A90F`, and the scroll down `$ADB9` (RickY $EAAE >= `$CC`) or up `$ADF0` (RickY < `$60`) unless Rick is dying (`$FD68`).
@about NewLife $E3AF starts every life: Rick alive and back to type 1, 6 bullets and 6 dynamite, Rick put back at the zone's restart point (`$AD29`), the HUD redrawn (`$A93D`). FrameTick $E49B is called by the IM 2 handler every frame and keeps a 32-bit frame count, which Random $E441 mixes in.
@about The pass counts (L1, the first instruction of MainLoop): c1 1073, controls 501, gameover 910, level1 2152, level2 2845, level3 2927, level4 1887; FrameTick, once an interrupt: c1 14301, level1 5822, level2 5870, so a pass takes about 2-3 frames in play.

$E3AF c NewLife ; A new life: Rick alive, ammo 6, back to the zone's restart point
> Clears the death flags `$FD69` (lose a life) and `$FD68` (Rick is dying), sets RickObject's type to 1, bullets `$A976` and dynamite `$A967` to 6, calls `$AD29` (Rick to the restart point of the zone) and `$A93D` (HUD), and falls into MainLoop $E3C9.
> Run 3 times in c1, 12 in level1 (one per life and new game), 29 in level4.
> Witness: L1 323 (beeper48, c1, controls, gameover, spotL3Z7-51, L1Z1-L1Z6, L2Z1-L2Z7, L3Z1-L3Z12, L4Z1-L4Z9, level1-level4, spotL1Z4-43).

$E3C9 c MainLoop ; The main loop, one pass every 2 frames in play
> Q (`$A13C` Z) quits to Quit $E35A. Then UpdateObjects $EC11, BonusCountdown $E466 (HL = RickY, unused), and the pause: P (`$A144` Z) waits for P to be let go, pressed again and let go (only c1 paused: 9228 / 139455 / 10050 polls).
> CheckDeath: when `$FD69` is set (Rick's death has played out, `$FC47`) one life `$A958` goes; none left: Quit $E35A, else NewLife $E3AF. The ZXDB infinite-lives POKE 58356,0 turns the `DEC A` at `$E3F4` into NOP (the warp recordings use it).
> CheckZone: when `$FD61` is set (Rick left the zone, `$FBD1` / `$FBE0`), `$AB93` changes the zone or level and CheckGameComplete $E406 follows; else MainLoopHalt.
> Witness: L1 43345 (beeper48, c1, controls, emptygun, ending2, gameover, l1end, l1z1left, spotL2Z4-34, spotL3Z7-51, spotL4Z8-69, L1Z1-L1Z6, L2Z1-L2Z7, L3Z1-L3Z12, L4Z1-L4Z9, level1-level4, spotL1Z4-43, spotL1Z4-44, spotL1Z4-47).
$E3DC PauseRelease ; P pressed: wait for its release
$E3E1 PauseWaitPress
$E3E6 PauseResume
$E3EB CheckDeath
$E3F4 ; POKE 58356,0 (infinite lives) makes this a NOP
$E3FD CheckZone

$E406 c CheckGameComplete ; After a zone change: the game complete, or the frame's drawing
> GameComplete $E440 set (`$AC52`, after the closing text of the ending) goes to GameOver $E35D (seen in ending); else back to MainLoop $E3C9.
> MainLoopHalt is the frame's HALT, reached from CheckZone when no zone change is pending. After it: `$A237` = 0, `$A73F`, `$A144`, `$A22A` (C = 1), `$A25D`, `$A90F`, then the vertical scroll unless `$FD68` (Rick dying): RickY $EAAE >= `$CC`: `$ADB9` (c1 14, level1 15); RickY < `$60`: `$ADF0` (only level2, 11 times).
> Witness: L1 106 (c1, ending2, l1end, L1Z2-L1Z4, L1Z6, L2Z2-L2Z7, L3Z2-L3Z12, L4Z2-L4Z6, L4Z8, level1).
$E40F MainLoopHalt ; the frame's HALT
$E437 CheckScrollUp
$E43E MainLoopNext

$E440 b GameComplete 1 ; $FF when the last level is done (`$AC52`); cleared by NewGame $E2DC
> Read by CheckGameComplete $E406. The ending recording sets it at the end of the closing text.

$E441 c Random ; A pseudo-random byte from the frame count
> HL = RandomState + FrameCount + `$0D` + FrameCountHigh (with carry); L = A XOR L XOR D XOR E XOR H (A the caller's), stored back to RandomState; returns that byte in A, HL and DE kept.
> Called by `$F4AA`; run in c1 (3) and levels 1-4 (19, 32, 13, 137). What the caller does with it is known only from the code.
> Witness: L1 519 (c1, L1Z3, L1Z4, L2Z2-L2Z5, L3Z2, L3Z5, L3Z11, L4Z1-L4Z3, L4Z5, L4Z7, L4Z8, level1-level4).

$E460 w RandomState 1 ; the generator's 16-bit state
$E462 FrameCount ; frames since the load, low word (FrameTick $E49B)
$E464 FrameCountHigh ; its high word

@module hud ; The bonus countdown
@about A bonus count of five decimal digits that runs while `$FD6C` is set. The start marker object (kind 22, `$F4C8`) sets `$FD6C` and the digits to 0 2 0 0 0 with effect 10; BonusCountdown $E466 takes 1 off the fourth digit every 30 passes; the end marker (kind 23, `$F502`) adds what is left to the score (`$A9E8` with DE = the last digit) and plays tune 7.

$E466 c BonusCountdown ; Count the bonus down while it runs
> Returns at once when `$FD6C` is 0. Else BonusDivider $E495 counts passes; every `$1E` passes (the reload) it takes 1 from BonusDigits+3 with a decimal borrow (a digit going below 0 becomes 9 and borrows from the one before); at 0 0 0 0 0 it stops.
> Run in c1, controls, gameover, level1 and level2; never in level3 / level4. Known only from the code: the digits are not drawn here.
> Witness: L1 43339 (beeper48, c1, controls, emptygun, ending2, gameover, l1end, l1z1left, spotL2Z4-34, spotL3Z7-51, spotL4Z8-69, L1Z1-L1Z6, L2Z1-L2Z7, L3Z1-L3Z12, L4Z1-L4Z9, level1-level4, spotL1Z4-43, spotL1Z4-44, spotL1Z4-47).
$E48B BonusDecrement
$E48E BonusBorrowLoop

$E495 b BonusDivider 6 ; passes to the next step ($1E reload; $32 in the image), then the five digits
> Written by BonusCountdown $E466 (BonusDivider and the digits) and by the start marker `$F4C8` (`$F4EE`-`$F4F9`: the digits); read by the end marker `$F502` (`$F529`: DE = BonusDigits+4).
$E496 BonusDigits ; five decimal digits, most significant first

@module mainloop
$E49B c FrameTick ; The 32-bit frame count, from the IM 2 handler
> FrameCount $E462 + 1, carried into FrameCountHigh $E464. Called by the IM 2 handler once a frame (its counts equal the handler's: c1 14301, ending 1499).
> Witness: L1 111926 (beeper48, c1, controls, emptygun, ending2, gameover, l1end, l1z1left, spotL2Z4-34, spotL3Z7-51, spotL4Z8-69, L1Z1-L1Z6, L2Z1-L2Z7, L3Z1-L3Z12, L4Z1-L4Z9, level1-level4, spotL1Z4-43, spotL1Z4-44, spotL1Z4-47).

$E4AD b Level 1 ; The level, 0-3; 4 after the last (the ending)
> Cleared by NewGame $E2DC, raised by the level change `$ABF6`; `$AC07` uses it to pick the LevelTable record, `$AC20` as the end-of-level tune.

@module levels
$E4AE b LevelTable 11 ; 11 bytes a level: 0 jungle, 1 Egypt, 2 castle, 3 missile base, 4 the ending
> +0-1 the intro text, +2-3 its screen address, +4 the attribute stored in `$7900`, +5 Rick's x (RickX $EAAD), +6-7 Rick's y (RickY $EAAE), +8-9 the first zone record (to IX), +10 the first view row, passed in C to LoadScreen `$AC83`, which stores it in ViewTopRow $ADB7 (not a zone count).
> Record 0 is read by NewGame $E2DC and StartLevel $E32C; at a level change `$AC07` reads record Level $E4AD (`$AC56`). The ending's record has only the text and the attribute in use. The warp recordings copy record N over record 0 (WALKTHROUGH 6.0).
@res levels/leveltable.bin include
$E4AE LevelTextPtr
$E4B0 LevelTextAt
$E4B2 LevelAttr
$E4B3 LevelRickX
$E4B4 LevelRickY
$E4B6 LevelZone
$E4B8 LevelViewTop
$E4B9 ; level 1: Egypt
$E4C4 ; level 2: Europe, the castle
$E4CF ; level 3: Europe, the missile base
$E4DA ; 4: the ending (London)

@module text ; The texts
@about The game's own character codes: `$FF` a new line, `$FE` the end of a text (`$AAE9`; GAME OVER's `$AA8D` stops at `$FF`). Digits are `$37` + the digit ('8' = 1, '9' = 2, '?' = 8, '@' = 9), '^' is a comma, '_' a full stop, '`' a question mark, 'C' before the year is a plain C (glyph 12); the font has no copyright sign.
@about The five intro and closing texts are printed by NewGame $E2DC and the level change `$AC1A`; the three menu texts by Menu $E219.

$E4E5 t SouthAmericaText ; Level 1 intro: South America, the Goolu tribe
@res texts/SouthAmericaText.bin
$E5FC t EgyptText ; Level 2 intro: Egypt, the jewel of Ankhel
@res texts/EgyptText.bin
$E70A t CastleText ; Level 3 intro: Europe, Schwarzendumpf castle
@res texts/CastleText.bin
$E80E t MissileBaseText ; Level 4 intro: Europe, the secret missile base
@res texts/MissileBaseText.bin
$E8F9 t LondonText ; The ending: London, the Barfian empire
@res texts/LondonText.bin
$E9FB t TitleText ; " R I C K    D A N G E R O U S "
@res texts/TitleText.bin
$EA1B t ControlsText ; 1 KEYBOARD, 2 KEMPSTON, 3 CURSOR, 4 SINCLAIR
@res texts/ControlsText.bin
$EA51 t CreditsText ; PRESS FIRE TO START and the two copyright lines
@res texts/CreditsText.bin

@module objects ; The objects: the table, the update, the enemies, traps and bonuses
@about ObjectTable $EA8E has 12 slots of 30 bytes and an `$FF` end. Slot 0 is read apart by `$F556`, `$F629` and `$F812`; slot 1 is Rick (RickObject $EAAC, kind 1, `$F851`), slot 2 his bullet (BulletObject $EACA, kind 2), slot 3 his dynamite (DynamiteObject $EAE8, kind 3); slots 4-11 (ZoneObjects $EB06) take the zone's objects (`$AC83`).
@about A record: +0 type (bit 7: a trap is deadly, or a box was hit; bits 0-6 the kind; 0 a free slot), +1 x (0-`$E8`), +2-3 y (16-bit), +4-5 the sprite frame, +6 mirror (`$FF` / 0), +7 width, +8 height, +9-10 the level object list entry (bit 7 of the byte after it: done), +11 flags, +12 the patrol length, +15 x and +16-17 y of the path start, +18-19 the frame base or the animation list, +20-21 the path start, +22-23 the path pointer, +24 the animation step or the walk step, +25 the path step count or the patrol count, +26 y fraction, +27-28 y speed (8.8, `$80` gravity a pass, at most `$0800`), +29 the stun count.
@about +11 flags: bit 0 one-shot (MarkObjectDone $EDDC when killed or ended), bit 2 the restarted path is deadly, bit 3 a triggered path is deadly, bit 4 the dynamite's blast triggers it, bit 5 the bullet, bit 6 the stick, bit 7 Rick's centre inside its box (`$F7C3`). +13 and +14 are not read in this fragment.
@about UpdateObjects $EC11 dispatches each slot's kind: `$47` DyingEnemyObj $F1B7, `$18` and up TrapObj $EDFC, else ObjectHandlers $EC47: 0 KillObject, 1 Rick, 2 BulletObj, 3 DynamiteObj, 4/7/10/13 PatrolObj $EFCF, 5/8/11/14 TrackerObj $EFD6, 6/9/12/15 ClimberObj $F233, 16/17 AmmoBoxObj $ED43, 18-21 TreasureObj $EDE6, 22/23 the bonus markers `$F4C8` / `$F502`.

$EA8E b ObjectTable 30 ; 12 object slots of 30 bytes, all 0 at the load
> The record format is in the module header. In play (work/images/play.*.bin) slot 1 is `01 8E A5 00 FD 84 01 18 15`: Rick, x `$8E`, y `$00A5`, frame `$84FD`, width `$18`, height `$15`.
$EAAC RickObject ; slot 1: Rick
$EAAD RickX
$EAAE RickY ; 16-bit
$EAB2 RickMirror ; +6
$EAB3 RickWidth
$EAB4 RickHeight
$EACA BulletObject ; slot 2: Rick's bullet
$EACB BulletX
$EACC BulletY
$EAE8 DynamiteObject ; slot 3: Rick's dynamite
$EAE9 DynamiteX
$EB06 ZoneObjects ; slots 4-11: the zone's objects
$EBF6 ObjectTableEnd ; $FF

$EBF7 c ResetObjects ; Free every slot but Rick's; no blast, no stick
> Every slot whose type is not 1 gets type 0, up to the `$FF` end; BlastOn $ECF1 and the stick flag `$FD63` are cleared. Called at each zone set-up (c1 7, level1 19, level4 30).
> Witness: L1 439 (beeper48, c1, controls, gameover, spotL3Z7-51, L1Z1-L1Z6, L2Z1-L2Z7, L3Z1-L3Z12, L4Z1-L4Z9, level1-level4, spotL1Z4-43).
$EC05 ResetObjectsLoop
$EC0E ResetObjectsNext

$EC11 c UpdateObjects ; Run every object's handler once
> IX = ObjectTable $EA8E; UpdateObjectSlot $EC15 per slot. Called once a pass by MainLoop $E3C9.
> Witness: L1 43340 (beeper48, c1, controls, emptygun, ending2, gameover, l1end, l1z1left, spotL2Z4-34, spotL3Z7-51, spotL4Z8-69, L1Z1-L1Z6, L2Z1-L2Z7, L3Z1-L3Z12, L4Z1-L4Z9, level1-level4, spotL1Z4-43, spotL1Z4-44, spotL1Z4-47).

$EC15 c UpdateObjectSlot ; One slot: dispatch on its kind
> Type 0 is skipped, `$FF` ends. Else NextObject $EC3B is pushed as the return address and the kind (type AND `$7F`) chosen: `$47` DyingEnemyObj $F1B7, `$18` and up TrapObj $EDFC, else the word ObjectHandlers[kind].
> Witness: L1 563418 (beeper48, c1, controls, emptygun, ending2, gameover, l1end, l1z1left, spotL2Z4-34, spotL3Z7-51, spotL4Z8-69, L1Z1-L1Z6, L2Z1-L2Z7, L3Z1-L3Z12, L4Z1-L4Z9, level1-level4, spotL1Z4-43, spotL1Z4-44, spotL1Z4-47).

$EC3B c NextObject ; IX to the next slot, +30
> Witness: L1 520078 (beeper48, c1, controls, emptygun, ending2, gameover, l1end, l1z1left, spotL2Z4-34, spotL3Z7-51, spotL4Z8-69, L1Z1-L1Z6, L2Z1-L2Z7, L3Z1-L3Z12, L4Z1-L4Z9, level1-level4, spotL1Z4-43, spotL1Z4-44, spotL1Z4-47).

$EC42 c KillObject ; Kind 0 with bit 7 set: free the slot
> ObjectHandlers $EC47 entry 0. Only a type `$80` reaches it. Run by no recording.
> Witness: L1 0 ().

$EC47 w ObjectHandlers 1 ; Handler of each kind 0-23
> Indexed by UpdateObjectSlot $EC15 with type AND `$7F` below `$18`.

@module rick ; Rick's bullet and dynamite as objects
@about Rick's own moves (`$F851`), his firing (`$FA39`-`$FA83`), the stick (`$F9DE`-`$FA1A`) and the dynamite drop (`$FA9C`-`$FAB7`) lie in the next fragment; this one holds the bullet and the dynamite once they are out, and the variables the enemies and traps test.

$EC77 c DynamiteObj ; Kind 3: the dynamite's fuse and blast
> DynFuse $ECED counts down by 1 a pass from the value the drop `$FAB1` gives it. While 20 or more the stick of dynamite shows FuseFrames $ECF2, mirrored every other pass; at 20 effect 2 (the bang, `$EC93`); below 20 the blast: BlastX $ECEE = x + 12, BlastY $ECEF = y + 10, BlastOn $ECF1 = `$FF`, the frame BlastFrames[fuse / 4]. While the fuse is 4 or more `$F76F` tests Rick (IX = RickObject) and kills him (`$FBED`) inside the blast. At 0 the slot and BlastOn are cleared.
> Run in level2 (50 passes) and level3 (300): the dynamite used there. The blast kills enemies (EnemyCommon), destroys boxes and triggers traps with flag bit 4.
> Witness: L1 1523 (beeper48, L1Z1, L1Z2, L2Z1, L2Z2, L2Z6, L2Z7, L3Z2, L3Z6, L3Z11, L3Z12, L4Z x5, level2, level3).
$EC85 DynamiteTick
$EC97 DynamiteFuseFrame
$ECA2 DynamiteBlast
$ECC5 DynamiteSetFrame

$ECED b DynFuse 1 ; the dynamite's fuse count (set by the drop `$FAB1`)
$ECEE b BlastX 1 ; the blast's centre x
$ECEF w BlastY 1 ; the blast's centre y
$ECF1 b BlastOn 1 ; $FF while the blast lasts; cleared by ResetObjects $EBF7, `$AD50` and DynamiteObj $EC77
$ECF2 w FuseFrames 1 ; the burning stick (twice), then BlastFrames
$ECF6 BlastFrames ; the five blast frames: small, large, larger, large, small (also the boxes' explosion)

$ED00 c BulletObj ; Kind 2: Rick's bullet flies until it hits a wall or leaves
> x += BulletDx $ED3F (signed: `$FA75` / `$FA83` set it when Rick fires); off the left edge or at `$E8` and up the bullet goes. BulletHitX $ED40 = x (left) or x + `$17` (right), BulletHitY $ED41 = y + 5. `$F535` probes the map there: a wall frees the slot. The enemies, boxes and traps test BulletX / BulletY or BulletHitX / BulletHitY with `$F742`.
> Run in c1 and levels 1-4 (25 to 84 passes).
> Witness: L1 546 (beeper48, c1, emptygun, L1Z5, L2Z1, L2Z6, L3Z x7, L4Z3, L4Z4, L4Z8, L4Z9, level1-level4).
